[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4584666068","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119901#issuecomment-4584666068","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119901","id":4584666068,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABEURz1A","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-30T20:48:28Z","updated_at":"2026-05-30T20:48:28Z","body":"The color shouldn't be read back to the CPU at all since this creates a sync point between the CPU and GPU. Instead you need to cache the color value in a buffer (could just be a 16 byte SSBO) and then use a compute shader to initialize the new buffer to that color value. ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4584666068/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4585029018","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119901#issuecomment-4585029018","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119901","id":4585029018,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABEUn9mg","user":{"login":"almic","id":21991767,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTkxNzY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21991767?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic","html_url":"https://github.com/almic","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-30T22:27:23Z","updated_at":"2026-05-30T22:27:23Z","body":"> The color shouldn't be read back to the CPU at all since this creates a sync point between the CPU and GPU. Instead you need to cache the color value in a buffer (could just be a 16 byte SSBO) and then use a compute shader to initialize the new buffer to that color value.\r\n\r\nThis is \"technically best,\" however consider the context. This is already during sync point as we are in the middle of preparing the next frame, and the user is resizing the window, so user input and frame-rate are usually not relevant. Also reading from the CPU isn't that terrible, given it is 4 bytes, and especially since the code is already destroying and creating several buffers at the same time.\r\n\r\nIf this is really necessary, then it could be to just save a boolean to copy the old current buffer into the new current buffer as part of the next frame, and then destroy the old buffer afterwards. It feels a little \"premature optimization\" to worry about. If any of my assumptions are wrong, please correct me.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4585029018/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4585117069","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119901#issuecomment-4585117069","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119901","id":4585117069,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABEUtVjQ","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-30T23:13:45Z","updated_at":"2026-05-30T23:13:45Z","body":"Your assumptions are wrong, this isn't a sync point already. Resizing Viewports doesn't require any special synchronization. Anything done on the GPU at run time needs to be fast. A CPU read back will stall the CPU for two frames. 30ms for this is unacceptably slow. Freeing and allocating the buffers is indeed slow, but it will be less than 1 ms, so it's a completely different order of magnitude. Ultimately, stalling on any operation that can be expected at run time is unacceptable in a real time renderer. \r\n\r\nCopying the current buffer over is fine if you would like to do it that way. I think it will just make managing lifetimes a little more tricky. So using a little SSBO may just make the code simpler. ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4585117069/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4585133005","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119901#issuecomment-4585133005","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119901","id":4585133005,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABEUuTzQ","user":{"login":"almic","id":21991767,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTkxNzY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21991767?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic","html_url":"https://github.com/almic","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-30T23:22:15Z","updated_at":"2026-05-30T23:34:25Z","body":"> Copying the current buffer over is fine if you would like to do it that way. I think it will just make managing lifetimes a little more tricky. So using a little SSBO may just make the code simpler.\r\n\r\nI went ahead and started writing my idea and found that I can't be sure if `free_data()` is only being called just prior to a `configure()` call, so it doesn't know if it should hold onto the final current buffer or not. Do you think a deferred call would be acceptable there to be sure it is freed soon, but not right away? What is your idea, I don't understand what you mean by SSBO.\r\n\r\nEDIT: Just had to use my brain a little, we can just replace the clear call with a copy call and it should be safe to destroy the extra buffer in the destructor of Luminance. Is that correct?\r\n\r\nEDIT 2: Nevermind, Luminance does not keep track of the buffers like that.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4585133005/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4585184690","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119901#issuecomment-4585184690","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119901","id":4585184690,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABEUxdsg","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-30T23:50:54Z","updated_at":"2026-05-30T23:50:54Z","body":"> What is your idea, I don't understand what you mean by SSBO.\r\n\r\nSSBO stands for Shader Storage Buffer Object. It is a general purpose buffer that you can read from and write to in shaders.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4585184690/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4585199786","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119901#issuecomment-4585199786","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119901","id":4585199786,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABEUyYqg","user":{"login":"almic","id":21991767,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTkxNzY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21991767?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic","html_url":"https://github.com/almic","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-30T23:58:04Z","updated_at":"2026-05-30T23:58:04Z","body":"> SSBO stands for Shader Storage Buffer Object. It is a general purpose buffer that you can read from and write to in shaders.\r\n\r\nI understand what they do, I just couldn't think of it immediately how that helps with them not existing long enough to be used between the call on `free_data()` and `configure()`. Now I think I see, Luminance can keep a SSBO and provide it to the buffers with their index, Luminance frees the SSBO in the destructor. Buffers read their index whenever they configure to obtain the color, and copy it just before they free. Does this sound right to you?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4585199786/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4587125013","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119901#issuecomment-4587125013","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119901","id":4587125013,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABEWn5FQ","user":{"login":"almic","id":21991767,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTkxNzY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21991767?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic","html_url":"https://github.com/almic","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-31T15:16:32Z","updated_at":"2026-05-31T15:16:32Z","body":"I have updated this to avoid the CPU read, instead the buffer is kept around. I still think it's wrong to retain a buffer after `free_data()`, but I don't see a simpler solution. My thought to have Luminance track a storage buffer would leave a lot of line changes for the same effect, and still require a destructor from LuminanceBuffers so that Luminance couldn't infinitely grow a buffer on the GPU. So I settled to just rely on the LuminanceBuffer destructor to clean up the retained `last_luminance` buffer.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4587125013/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4752804269","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119901#issuecomment-4752804269","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119901","id":4752804269,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABG0oJrQ","user":{"login":"almic","id":21991767,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTkxNzY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21991767?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic","html_url":"https://github.com/almic","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-19T15:21:15Z","updated_at":"2026-06-19T15:21:15Z","body":"@clayjohn This is ready to be reviewed again","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4752804269/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4762426459","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119901#issuecomment-4762426459","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119901","id":4762426459,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABG9zcWw","user":{"login":"almic","id":21991767,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTkxNzY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21991767?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic","html_url":"https://github.com/almic","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almic/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-21T15:25:11Z","updated_at":"2026-06-21T15:25:11Z","body":"The API for texture copy with 2d textures changed.\r\n\r\nOld:\r\n> Copies the `from_texture` to `to_texture` with the specified `from_pos`, `to_pos` and `size` coordinates. The Z axis of the `from_pos`, `to_pos` and `size` must be `0` for 2-dimensional textures.\r\n\r\nNew:\r\n> Copies the `from_texture` to `to_texture` with the specified `from_pos`, `to_pos` and `size` coordinates. For 2-dimensional textures, `from_pos` and `to_pos` must have a Z axis of `0`, and `size` must have a Z axis of `1`.\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4762426459/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]